1. Create an instance of the AEAD GCM cipher class.
2. Initialize the cipher with the desired encryption or decryption mode, as well as the secret key and any other necessary parameters.
3. Use the `updateAAD` method to add the AAD to the cipher's context. This can be done by calling the method with the AAD data as an argument.
4. Encrypt or decrypt the data using the cipher's `encrypt` or `decrypt` methods, respectively. The AAD will be included in the encrypted or decrypted data, providing authentication and integrity protection.

