To create a NestJS model that creates a MongoDB document containing multiple schemas, follow these steps:

1. Install required packages:

```bash
npm install @nestjs/mongodb mongoose
```

2. Create a `model.ts` file in your NestJS project directory and define your Mongoose model:

```typescript
// model.ts
import { Model, Schema, Document } from 'mongoose';

interface User extends Document {
  name: string;
  age: number;
  addresses: Address[];
}

interface Address extends Document {
  street: string;
  city: string;
  state: string;
}

const userSchema = new Schema({
  name: String,
  age: Number,
  addresses: [Address],
});

const addressSchema = new Schema({
  street: String,
  city: String,
  state: String,
});

export const UserModel: Model<User> = model('User', userSchema);
export const AddressModel: Model<Address> = model('Address', addressSchema);
```

