3. Call the function for each character and append the resulting Morse Code representation to a string.
4. Return the final Morse Code representation string.

Here's an example of how you can implement this approach in MATLAB:

```matlab
function morse_code = encode_morse(char)
    % Define the Morse Code representation table
    morse_code_table = {'.-', '-...', '-.-.', '-..', '.', '..-', '--.', '....', '..', '.---', '-.', '.-..', '--', '-.', '---', '.--.', '--.-', '.-', '...', '-', '..-', '...-', '.--', '-..-', '-.--', '--..'};

    % Look up the Morse Code representation for the given character
    morse_code = morse_code_table{strfind(char, '')};
end

% Test the function with a sample phrase
input_phrase = 'HELLO';
output_morse_code = '';
