Natural selection can be modeled using MATLAB. Here's a simple example:

```MATLAB
% Define population parameters
population_size = 100;
mutation_rate = 0.01;
selection_pressure = 0.5;

% Initialize population
population = randi([0 1], population_size, 1);

% Simulate evolution over time
for i = 1:100
    % Compute fitness based on selection pressure
    fitness = population .* selection_pressure;

    % Apply mutation
    mutated_population = population .+ mutation_rate .* randn(population_size, 1);

    % Select new population based on fitness
    new_population = mutated_population(fitness > rand(population_size));

    % Update population for next iteration
    population = new_population;
end

% Plot the evolution of the population
figure;
plot(1:100, mean(population));
xlabel('Generation');
ylabel('Fitness');
title('Evolution under Natural Selection');
```

