To set up Auth0 SSO (Single Sign-On) for multiple React apps, follow these steps:

1. Create an Auth0 account and configure your first application.
2. In the Auth0 dashboard, go to the "Applications" tab and click on the "Create Application" button.
3. Choose "Web App" as the application type and fill in the required information, such as the application name, logo, and callback URL.
4. Under "Advanced Settings," enable the "Enable Single Sign-On (SSO)" option and select the "SAML 2.0" protocol.
5. Copy the "Issuer URL" and "X.509 Certificate" from the Auth0 dashboard.
6. Install the `@auth0/auth0-react` package in your React app using npm or yarn:
```bash
npm install @auth0/auth0-react
```
or
```bash
yarn add @auth0/auth0-react
```
7. Import the `Auth0Provider` component from the `@auth0/auth0-react` package in your app's entry point (e.g., `src/index.js`) and wrap your app with it:
```javascript
import { Auth0Provider } from '@auth0/auth0-react';

const domain = 'your-domain.com'; // Replace with your Auth0 domain
const clientId = 'your-client-id'; // Replace with your Auth0 client ID

function App() {
  return (
    <Auth0Provider
      domain={domain}
      clientId={clientId}
      redirectUri={window.location.origin}
      onRedirectCallback={(appState) => console.log(appState)}
    >
      {/* Your app content goes here */}
    </Auth0Provider>
  );
}

export default App;
```
Replace `your-domain.com` with your Auth0 domain and `your-client-id` with your Auth0 client ID.

8. In each of your React apps, import the `Auth0Provider` component and wrap your app with it, using the same `domain`, `clientId`, and `redirectUri` values.

