Here's the R code to check if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric:

```R
function is_numeric(x) {
  tryCatch({
    as.numeric(x)
    TRUE
  }, error = function(e) FALSE)
}

vector <- c("1", "2", "3", NA, "4")
all_numeric <- sapply(vector[!is.na(vector)], is_numeric)
print(all_numeric)
```

This code defines a function `is_numeric()` that attempts to convert a character string to numeric using `as.numeric()`. If the conversion is successful, the function returns `TRUE`, otherwise it returns `FALSE`. The `sapply()` function is then used to apply the `is_numeric()` function to each element of the `vector` that is not NA. The resulting boolean vector indicates whether each element can be converted to numeric or not.

```R
is_numeric_vector <- function(x) {
  tryCatch({
    is.numeric(x[!is.na(x)])
  }, error = function(e) FALSE)
}
```

```R
is_all_numeric <- function(x) {
  is.numeric(unlist(lapply(x, as.numeric)))
}

# Example usage
x <- c("1", "2", "3", NA, "4")
if (is_all_numeric(x)) {
  print("All non-NA elements in x can be converted to numeric.")
} else {
  print("Not all non-NA elements in x can be converted to numeric.")
}
```

