This decorator will only allow the `getData` method to be executed if the `NODE_ENV` variable is set to 'true'. If it's set to any other value, the method will return `false` and the request will be denied.

Here's a decorator for Nest.js middleware that checks the NODE_ENV variable and returns `next()` if it's set to `true`, otherwise, it returns `false`.

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';
import { Observable } from 'rxjs';
import { catchError, map, tap } from 'rxjs/operators';

@Injectable()
export class EnvironmentMiddleware {
  constructor() {}

  use(middleware: any): Observable<any> {
    return middleware.pipe(
      tap((data) => {
        if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'true') {
          return data;
        } else {
          return false;
        }
      }),
      catchError((error) => error),
      map((data) => data),
    );
  }
}
```

To use this middleware, you can inject it into your controller or service and use it as follows:

```typescript
import { Controller, Get } from '@nestjs/common';
import { EnvironmentMiddleware } from './environment.middleware';

@Controller('example')
export class ExampleController {
  constructor(private readonly environmentMiddleware: EnvironmentMiddleware) {}

  @Get()
  async getData(): Promise<any> {
    const data = await this.environmentMiddleware.use(async () => {
      // Your business logic here
      return { message: 'Hello, World!' };
    });

    if (data) {
      return data;
    } else {
      return { message: 'Environment is not in development mode.' };
    }
  }
}
```

In this example, the `getData` method uses the `use` method of the `EnvironmentMiddleware` class to wrap the asynchronous function that fetches the data. The middleware checks the NODE_ENV variable and returns the data if it's set to `true`, otherwise, it returns `false`. If `false` is returned, the `getData` method returns a different message indicating that the environment is not in development mode.

```typescript
import { Injectable, CanActivate, ExecutionContext } from '@nestjs/common';

@Injectable()
export class EnvironmentMiddleware implements CanActivate {
  canActivate(context: ExecutionContext): boolean {
    const request = context.switchToHttp().getRequest();
    const nodeEnv = process.env.NODE_ENV;

    if (nodeEnv === 'true') {
      return true;
    } else {
      return false;
    }
  }
}
```

